      "title": "epan: Add a comment about trailing stray character detection",
      "message": "epan: Add a comment about trailing stray character detection\n\nTrailing stray character detection should happen before the\nconversion to UTF-8. Not only would that make it possible to\ndetect stray characters for more encodings (that change string\nlength after conversion), we should be doing it for ASCII and\nUTF-8 too because substituting REPLACEMENT CHARACTERS for illegal\ncharacters can change those lengths.\n\nIn the worst case, a UTF-8 string that has many 4 byte sequences\nthat almost look like valid 4 byte characters but fail on the last\none can actually get shorter if those sequences are replaced by\n3 byte REPLACEMENT CHARACTERS, which can mean illegal memory\naccess in detect_trailing_stray_characters.\n\nRelated to #18945\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
